# Veyrune — Environment Variables

Copy to `.env` (local) or set in Secret Manager / Cloud Run (production).
Nothing here is required for local dev with defaults — SQLite + no LLM works
and degrades honestly.

## Core
| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | `production` enforces secret requirements |
| `STORAGE_BACKEND` | `sqlite` | `firestore` in production |
| `SQLITE_DB_PATH` | `data/agentos.db` | local only |
| `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` | — | required for Firestore/Vertex |
| `GOOGLE_CLOUD_REGION` | `us-central1` | Vertex location |
| `FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID` | `(default)` | |

## LLM (order of fallback: Gemini → Vertex → Groq → xAI → HuggingFace)
| Variable | Notes |
|---|---|
| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | server-level key; users can add their own in Settings |
| `GEMINI_MODEL` | default `gemini-3.8-flash` |
| `GEMINI_ALLOWED_MODELS` | CSV whitelist |
| `GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL` | `gemini-embedding-001` |
| `GROQ_API_KEY` / `GROQ_MODEL` | fallback provider |
| `XAI_API_KEY` / `HF_TOKEN` | further fallbacks |

## Security (production requires these)
| Variable | Notes |
|---|---|
| `SECRETS_MASTER_KEY` | AES-256-GCM vault key — Secret Manager `secrets-master-key` |
| `JWT_PRIVATE_KEY` / `JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` | RS256 PEMs — Secret Manager; or PEM files on disk |
| `JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES` | default 15 |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | frontend URL(s), comma-separated |
| `FRONTEND_BASE_URL` | used for OAuth redirect defaults |

## Rate limiting (per process; multiply by instances or use a gateway)
| Variable | Default |
|---|---|
| `RATE_LIMIT_AUTH` | 20/min |
| `RATE_LIMIT_WORKFLOW` | 10/min |
| `RATE_LIMIT_MCP_BUILD` | 10/min |
| `RATE_LIMIT_GENERAL` | 60/min |

## Budgets & retention
| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `DEFAULT_DAILY_TOKEN_LIMIT` | 1,000,000 | per user; hard stop at 0 remaining |
| `MODEL_COST_PER_1M_TOKENS` | `gemini-3.8-flash:0.60,...` | estimate pricing, `model:rate` CSV |
| `RETENTION_DAYS` | 90 | 0 disables purging of events/audit rows |
| `HEALTH_USER_AGENT` | browser-compatible | site-health probe UA |

## Observability
| Variable | Notes |
|---|---|
| `SENTRY_DSN` | enables Sentry when set |

## Shared browser runtime

| Variable | Notes |
|---|---|
| `AGENTOS_BROWSER_INTERNAL_TOKEN` | Shared secret-store reference/value injected into API and browser-owning workers; required when internal browser routing is enabled. |
| `AGENTOS_WORKFLOW_BROWSER_URL` | Compose workflow worker's advertised private origin, e.g. `http://worker:8082`. Set with the internal token to expose the actual WebAgent page to API replicas. |
| `AGENTOS_DEDICATED_BROWSER_URL` | Dedicated browser worker's private origin, e.g. `http://browser-worker:8082`. Each replica needs its own routable origin. |
| `AGENTOS_BROWSER_INTERNAL_URL` | Worker-level advertised origin; Compose derives it from the worker-specific variables above. |
| `AGENTOS_BROWSER_TRUSTED_ENDPOINTS` | Exact comma-separated private origins the API may route to. Must include the advertised worker origins. |
| `AGENTOS_BROWSER_BIND_HOST` | Internal listener bind address; defaults to `0.0.0.0`. Keep this port on the private service network. |

An empty worker URL disables the internal listener. It does not prove cross-replica
browser readiness. Configure unique replica origins and the shared token before
running the deployed takeover qualification journey.

## Managed MCP runner

| Variable | Notes |
|---|---|
| `AGENTOS_RUNNER_IMAGE_DIGEST` | Immutable local Docker image ID (`sha256:…`) for the dedicated minimal runtime. Generated code never runs in the application container. |
| `AGENTOS_RUNNER_PROFILE_DIGEST` | Approved isolation-profile identity. Configuration alone does not constitute deployment qualification. |
| `AGENTOS_RUNNER_DATABASE_URL` | Secret-store-injected PostgreSQL connection for the shared execution journal. Apply migration 0021 before starting the runner. |
| `AGENTOS_RUNNER_DATABASE_SCHEMA` | Journal schema; defaults to `public`. Must be a simple SQL identifier. |
| `AGENTOS_RUNNER_JOURNAL` | Alternative local SQLite journal path for a single runtime host. Do not set together with the PostgreSQL URL. |

The shared journal records the actual Docker engine identity. Another worker
can request cancellation, but only the owning engine may confirm cleanup.
Generated servers always have networking disabled. Explicit anonymous HTTPS
read grants use the supervised operation broker; credentialed reads and writes
are not enabled by these grants. See `docs/managed-mcp-builds.md`.
